From f15d888412d52466880f14a97ee252bd11acb150 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Upamanyu Sharma <sharma.upamanyu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:55:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] wal: return Create's cleanup error instead of panicking

When Create fails after renaming the WAL directory into place (opening,
fsyncing or closing the parent directory), cleanupWAL closes the WAL and
renames it to <dir>.broken.<timestamp>; a failure of that close or rename
called lg.Panic. cleanupWAL now returns the error and Create returns it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../storage/wal/create_cleanup_error_test.go  | 60 +++++++++++++++++++
 server/storage/wal/wal.go                     | 15 +++--
 2 files changed, 71 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 server/storage/wal/create_cleanup_error_test.go

diff --git a/server/storage/wal/create_cleanup_error_test.go b/server/storage/wal/create_cleanup_error_test.go
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..4cef957f2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/server/storage/wal/create_cleanup_error_test.go
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
